      <Comment source="O-27, pujar">A cDNA clone encoding a Fe(II) transporter gene was isolated from Fe-deficient roots of |FRAME: TAX-4527 &lt;i&gt;Oryza&lt;/i&gt;|. The cDNA was homologous to |FRAME: TAX-3701 &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis&lt;/i&gt;| IRT1. The cDNA was recombinantly expressed in yeast and the cDNA reversed the defects of yeast iron-uptake mutant. The mRNA was expressed in roots and induced by iron and Cu-deficiency |CITS: [12096107]|.</Comment>
